    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0073" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/839: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-09-06T13:00:00+03:00">September 6,
                            1941—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 6—11:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1631. The report of Lozovski’s<anchor n="28" xml:id="d75-f1"/> press conference
                    on September 4, states that an American correspondent inquired as to the truth
                    of a report that peace negotiations are being conducted between the Soviet Union
                    and Finland with the assistance of the Government of the United States. Lozovski
                    is said to have replied that “this report is not in accord with the facts, but
                    certain Finnish newspapers are raising the question of peace for Finland because
                    of the heavy Finnish losses on the front, the bad food situation in Finland, the
                    growing desire of the Finnish people for peace, and their increasing hatred of
                    Hitlerite Germany.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d75-f1" n="28" xml:id="d75-f1-content">
                <p>Solomon Abramovich Lozovsky, Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs of
                    the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
